%description:
Tests that a home agent intercepts packets addressed to an absent mobile node on the
mobile node's home link, as RFC 6275 Section 10.4.1 requires: while a home registration
binding exists, the home agent answers Neighbor Solicitations for the mobile node's home
address with its own link-layer address, and multicasts a Neighbor Advertisement on the
mobile node's behalf when it accepts the binding.

Two hosts sit on the home link and ping the mobile node's home address.

  EarlyHost starts before the mobile node leaves, so it holds a neighbour cache entry
  pointing at the mobile node's own link-layer address, and can only keep reaching it if
  that entry is replaced or discarded.

  LateHost starts after the mobile node has left, so it has no cache entry at all and must
  resolve the home address from scratch on the home link. Only a proxy reply to its
  Neighbor Solicitation can answer it.

The mobile node leaves the home link at about t=32s, the home agent accepts its Binding
Update at t=34.6s, and the mobile node is back on the home link from about t=76s (it
de-registers at t=78.1s). Replies are counted only for requests sent between t=36s and
t=75.5s, while the mobile node is away and registered, so a reply after its return cannot
satisfy the test.

  EarlyHost reaches the mobile node from t=36s on because the multicast takeover
  advertisement carries a set Override flag (RFC 6275 Section 10.4.1 requires it) and
  replaces its cached link-layer address with the home agent's.

  LateHost reaches it because the home agent answers its Neighbor Solicitations.

Without the interception neither host is answered in that window: EarlyHost sends to a
link-layer address nobody answers to, and LateHost loops on address resolution.

The withdrawal on the mobile node's return is asserted from the log.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: test.ned

import inet.node.ipv6.StandardHost6;
import inet.test.moduletest.lib.Mipv6Network;
import inet.test.moduletest.lib.ethernetline;

//
// The frozen Mipv6Network with two hosts added on the home link. The home link is the
// segment behind AP_Home, which bridges to the home agent, so the hosts, the home agent
// and the mobile node while it is at home all share one link.
//
network Mipv6ProxyNdNetwork extends Mipv6Network
{
    submodules:
        EarlyHost: StandardHost6 {
            @display("p=180,300");
        }
        LateHost: StandardHost6 {
            @display("p=180,380");
        }
    connections:
        EarlyHost.ethg++ <--> ethernetline <--> AP_Home.ethg++;
        LateHost.ethg++ <--> ethernetline <--> AP_Home.ethg++;
}

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
**.mipv6.cmdenv-log-level = trace
**.app[*].cmdenv-log-level = trace
**.Home_Agent.ipv6.neighbourDiscovery.cmdenv-log-level = info
**.*Host.ipv6.neighbourDiscovery.cmdenv-log-level = warn   # so a failed address resolution is reported
**.cmdenv-log-level = off
cmdenv-event-banners = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
network = Mipv6ProxyNdNetwork
sim-time-limit = 100s
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = "%C: "
num-rngs = 3
seed-set = 1
**.mobility.rng-0 = 2

# number of MNs and CNs
*.total_mn = 1
*.total_cn = 1

**.neighbourDiscovery.minIntervalBetweenRAs = 0.03s
**.neighbourDiscovery.maxIntervalBetweenRAs = 0.07s
**.neighbourDiscovery.detectL2Movement = false   # legacy: detect movement from periodic RAs only

# channel physical parameters
*.radioMedium.mediumLimitCache.maxTransmissionPower = 2.0mW
*.radioMedium.mediumLimitCache.minReceptionPower = -82dBm
*.radioMedium.mediumLimitCache.minInterferencePower = -82dBm

# access point
**.wlan*.mgmt.numAuthSteps = 4

# ALL APs common parameters
**.AP*.wlan*.mgmt.beaconInterval = 0.1s

# Access Point parameters
**.AP_Home.wlan*.mgmt.ssid = "HOME"
**.AP_Home.wlan*.address = "10:AA:00:00:00:01"
**.AP_Home.eth[0].address = "10:AE:00:00:00:02"
**.AP_Home.eth[0].duplexMode = true

**.AP_1.wlan*.mgmt.ssid = "AP1"
**.AP_1.wlan*.address = "10:AA:00:00:A1:01"
**.AP_1.eth[0].address = "10:AE:00:00:A1:02"
**.AP_1.eth[0].duplexMode = true

# mobility
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 0m

**.MN[0].mobility.typename = "RectangleMobility"
**.MN[0].mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 180m
**.MN[0].mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 170m
**.MN[0].mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 630m
**.MN[0].mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 180m
**.MN[0].mobility.startPos = 0
**.MN[0].mobility.speed = 10mps
**.MN*.mobility.updateInterval = 0.1s


# ip settings
**.forwarding = false

# Ethernet NIC configuration
**.eth[*].queue.typename = "EthernetQosQueue"
**.eth[*].queue.dataQueue.typename = "DropTailQueue"
**.eth[*].queue.dataQueue.packetCapacity = 10
**.eth*.duplexMode = true

# analog model
**.analogModel.ignorePartialInterference = true

# wireless channels
**.AP_Home.wlan*.radio.channelNumber = 1
**.AP_1.wlan*.radio.channelNumber = 2
**.MN*.wlan*.radio.channelNumber = 0

# wireless configuration
**.wlan*.agent.activeScan = true
**.wlan*.agent.defaultSsid = ""
**.wlan*.agent.channelsToScan = "1 2"
**.wlan*.agent.probeDelay = 0.1s
**.wlan*.agent.minChannelTime = 0.15s
**.wlan*.agent.maxChannelTime = 0.3s
**.wlan*.agent.authenticationTimeout = 5s
**.wlan*.agent.associationTimeout = 5s

# nic settings
**.wlan*.bitrate = 2Mbps
**.wlan*.mac.dcf.channelAccess.cwMin = 7
**.radio.transmitter.power = 2.0mW

**.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.constraintAreaMaxX = 850m
**.constraintAreaMaxY = 850m


# The home-link hosts ping the mobile node's home address. The address is hardcoded rather
# than resolved with "MN[0](ipv6)", which returns whichever address the mobile node happens
# to hold at resolution time -- its link-local address before autoconfiguration finishes,
# and its care-of address once it has moved away -- never reliably the stable home address.
**.MN*.numApps = 0
**.CN*.numApps = 0
*.EarlyHost.numApps = 1
*.LateHost.numApps = 1
**.EarlyHost.app[0].typename = "PingApp"
**.LateHost.app[0].typename = "PingApp"
**.*Host.app[0].destAddr = "aaaa:0:66:0:8aa:ff:fe00:8"
**.*Host.app[0].packetSize = 56B
**.*Host.app[0].hopLimit = 32
**.*Host.app[0].sendInterval = 0.5s
**.*Host.app[0].printPing = true

# before the mobile node leaves, so the cache entry is populated while it is still at home
**.EarlyHost.app[0].startTime = 1s
# after the home agent has accepted the binding, so address resolution starts from an empty cache
**.LateHost.app[0].startTime = 40s

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%subst: /omnetpp:://
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
Mipv6ProxyNdNetwork.Home_Agent.ipv6.mipv6: BU validation passed
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
Mipv6ProxyNdNetwork.Home_Agent.ipv6.neighbourDiscovery: Providing Neighbour Discovery proxy service for aaaa:0:66:0:8aa:ff:fe00:8
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%# LateHost starts at t=40s, 5 s after the home agent accepted the binding, so each of its
%# solicitations is answered. (EarlyHost fails once at t=4s, before any binding exists, while
%# the mobile node is still at home; that is not asserted.)
%postrun-command: grep "LateHost.ipv6.neighbourDiscovery: Address Resolution has failed" test.out > test_addrres.out || true
%not-contains: test_addrres.out
Address Resolution has failed
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%# The multicast takeover advertisement RFC 6275 Section 10.4.1 requires on accepting the
%# binding, sent for an address the home agent does not hold.
%contains: stdout
Mipv6ProxyNdNetwork.Home_Agent.ipv6.neighbourDiscovery: Sending unsolicited Neighbour Advertisement for aaaa:0:66:0:8aa:ff:fe00:8 on eth1 as a proxy
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%# ...and the withdrawal when the mobile node comes home and de-registers.
%contains: stdout
Mipv6ProxyNdNetwork.Home_Agent.ipv6.neighbourDiscovery: No longer providing Neighbour Discovery proxy service for aaaa:0:66:0:8aa:ff:fe00:8
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%# EarlyHost: requests sent from t=36s to t=75.5s are icmp_seq 70 to 149 (80 requests).
%postrun-command: awk '/EarlyHost.app\[0\]: reply of/ && match($0, /icmp_seq=[0-9]+/) { q = substr($0, RSTART+9, RLENGTH-9)+0; if (q >= 70 && q <= 149) n++ } END { print (n >= 70) ? "EARLY-REACHED-WHILE-AWAY" : "EARLY-ONLY-" n+0 }' test.out > test_early.out
%contains: test_early.out
EARLY-REACHED-WHILE-AWAY
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%# LateHost: requests sent from t=40s to t=75.5s are icmp_seq 0 to 71 (72 requests).
%postrun-command: awk '/LateHost.app\[0\]: reply of/ && match($0, /icmp_seq=[0-9]+/) { q = substr($0, RSTART+9, RLENGTH-9)+0; if (q <= 71) n++ } END { print (n >= 60) ? "LATE-RESOLVED-WHILE-AWAY" : "LATE-ONLY-" n+0 }' test.out > test_late.out
%contains: test_late.out
LATE-RESOLVED-WHILE-AWAY
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
